// FnRet.fol — package source file
// Spec: language-ref.md > Functions Taking and Returning Functions >
//       Syntax 2 — Named type alias
//
// The result-position half of the pair. A named function type is usable in
// either position, so the same alias mechanism covers "takes a function" and
// "returns a function".
//
// Note on the reference's `funtype co.lang.type = (a co.lang.int,
// b co.lang.int)->(co.lang.int);` — that spelling names the parameters inside
// a TYPE. The grammar's function type is `"(" [type-list] ")",
// return-type-clause`, and a type-list holds type expressions only, so these
// examples use the unnamed form. Parameter names belong to a declaration or an
// anonymous-function expression, not to a type.

_ co.lang.type = (co.lang.int)->(co.lang.int);
